---
description: TokenSQL remote development and reviewed OpenCode pricing maintenance
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow plan.md, AGENTS.md and docs/pricing_conditions_contract.md.
Official stable IDs, typed conditions and explicit discount scopes preserve raw data;
unknown is not all. Show zhe once; expand multi-item official prices without writes.
All project operations run remotely through ssh uni; never create local project
copies or write C-drive files. Never read handoff/private handoff or cleanup
backup business files. Do not alter shared inference or coding services.

Use one unique model_id with optional display name and aliases; physical_key
is removed. Quotes create missing models atomically, without a separate model
approval. Other business fields may be null. New omitted currency defaults to
CNY; explicit foreign currencies and null remain intact. Never guess token
scale, supplier or prices to pass schema.
Units preserve the original 12 IDs and add mtoken_hour/request/account_month
for three currencies (21 total); never treat these as token equivalents.
Preserve raw amounts and raw multipliers independently, including discount-only
records. Discount ratios are HALF_UP rounded to two decimal places in storage,
UI-derived results and exports (0.80 = 8 zhe, 0.15 = 1.5 zhe). Use deterministic
Decimal/BigInt code, never binary floats. Do not round amount/price/FX values;
existing-ratio migrations require backup, atomic revisions and before/after audit. All official-price discount/paid-price calculations are frontend-only,
exact executable code and exportable; never mutate raw stored data.

Frontend currency/unit controls, custom factors and converted exports are
display-only and cannot mutate stored raw prices, global context or memory.
Cross-dimensional estimates require clear assumptions, source/model,
resolution/FPS and a visible estimate label. Never claim a universal token/second.

OpenCode prepares proposals only. Human review confirms atomic audited writes;
Structured clarification questions use waiting_for_input, not failed. Resume
with the same job/session/files and revision check; isolate each attempt output,
refresh catalog, retain waiting across restart, and never commit or remember
while waiting. Real SDK/schema failures remain failures.
cancel returns files and creates no formal prices or memory. Selected quotes
are permanently deleted after one explicit UI confirmation, atomically with
revision validation and audit; never auto-delete production data in tests.
Do not restore
removed fixed parsing pipelines. Never automatically import samples/backups.
User-initiated official-price lookup uses a new scoped OpenCode session and
the official-source index, fetches primary evidence, then human-reviewed writes.
Confirmed corrections alone may become scoped memory outside the repository.

Root coordinates and independently verifies; coding/review Subagents use the
explicitly selected gpt-6.1-sol ultra; root uses Astra. Preserve unrelated changes.
Record actual evidence in progress.md; distinguish unit tests, API stubs,
real browser, real model and real business-file validation.
